From 3846e0623a2ff91ab6401aba097b5b37f2fbc6ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:32:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read charts as documents and sections, like an EHR

The text view found 3 of 17 sections on an ordinary H&P: it kept only
the first heading on each page, kept each label once per chart, read
'SOCIAL HISTORY: former smoker' as a field rather than a section, and
called any line starting 'Plan...' a heading.

A new parser reads the extracted text as documents (H&P, progress note,
consult, discharge summary...) made of sections, from a vocabulary of
about 45 sections in the spellings EHRs print, and a line is a heading
only when shaped like one. The viewer gains a navigator that follows
the reader, jumps to the exact heading, a side-by-side scan view, and
an optional highlight of uncertain-diagnosis and linkage wording. It
reopens a chart where the reader left it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
